<!--Post: 7263--><!--Time: 1108338224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7263"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Victoria<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victoria<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 3:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been thinking about these two. Jack the Ripper is still a mystery of enduring fascination. He has never been caught but wrote letters and indulged the public in his identity. <BR> <BR>Is BTK fashioning himself on JTR, a killer who has never been caught and still after 100 years is written about? <BR> <BR>The clues are part of BTK&#39;s history and, if the newspapers will not print photos, catchbtk.com will get a package eventually.   <BR> <BR>Like JTR, we will never find out who was BTK. However, we will need suspects.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7263-->
<!--Post: 7340--><!--Time: 1108409005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7340"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:witchkingofangmar@comcast.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 11:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Victoria-- <BR>I think there are many similaries between the two as well. I&#39;ve posted as such here. I think BTK WILL be caught and I also think this latest &#39;ego stroking by police taunting&#39; will one day lead to his downfall. I think what BTK fear most is up and having a heart attack like Zodiac &#40;Arthur Leigh Allen&#41; and just vanishing without a final send off for himself. <BR>Jack died in an asylum is my considered opinion and BTK may have had a recent health scare he though might leave his legacy unfulfilled by his own standards. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll know more soon. How&#39;s that for a teaser? <BR> <BR>Jack was found out but they lacked enough evidence to convict. Zodiac was found out but they lacked enough evidence to convict. BTK hasn&#39;t been caught and yet left DNA everywhere----this will be his final difference from his &#39;idols&#39;, capture<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7340-->
<!--Post: 7355--><!--Time: 1108421316-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7355"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 2:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->At least in the Ripper case they had suspects. The leading suspect that the investigators believed was responsible for the murders ended up in a mental hospital and died soon after. <BR>With the BTK case as far as we no there are no suspects. <BR>Had modern forensic and scientific tools been available at the time of the Ripper it would have no doubt been solved conclusively even if there was no trail. <BR>This is the 21st century with the perpetrator of a 20th century series of crimes still with us and taunting the police, media and public with no apparent significant lead to solve this.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7355-->
<!--Post: 7492--><!--Time: 1108519440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7492"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 6:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While Allen is a good Zodiac suspect, it&#39;s a stretch to say that he <b>was</b> Z.  If there wasn&#39;t enough evidence to convict him in a court of law, then there is technically no conclusive proof that he was Z.  But I do see what you&#39;re getting at.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7492-->
<!--Post: 7521--><!--Time: 1108550135-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7521"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Suspiria_2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Suspiria_2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 2:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->it seems odd to me that an large amount of people view btk as &#34;wanting to reveal his name before the end&#34;.  it jives with the egotism evinced, in a way, but it doesn&#39;t make sense when one observes what actually happens to serial killers once they become known. <BR> <BR>the reason that jack and zack &#40;or zodiac&#41; are still so talked about and widely speculated upon is that their true persons have never become known, and as time passes are less likely to be discovered.  in that way the public can do what it likes best-build up a mystique and legend around known facts convoluted with rumour and a generous dash of wild speculation.  in some ways i think the public are very much like small children who like to be spooked with flashlit tales around the campfire. <BR> <BR>after a killer is found, although notice is paid to the background and lifestyle of the killer in an attempt to figure out their motivations for the crimes they committed, the public quickly loses interest.  it is as if the real person is tried against the myth and found lacking.  especially when, as i believe ressler or douglas once observed, the killers themselves don&#39;t make for very photogenic or articulate personalities.  i believe they said &#34;you can&#39;t find out anything about them by talking to them.  interviewing them in person is a waste of time...&#34;  or something to that effect. <BR> <BR>i guess in my own windbaggish and disjointed way, i&#39;m saying that the best way for btk to ensure his legend is to never get caught.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7521-->
